    "description": "In 21 places on the South Shetland Islands, that experience similar annual\n      precipitation, the superficial concentration of Cs-137 was determined. For the\n      determination of the distribution, samples were collected a profile of 25 cm\n      for radiological analysis, and  to determine edaphic parameters for the layer,\n      1 - 1.5 kg samples ware taken for radiological analysis. For the edaphic\n      analysis, 4 cylinders of 305 ml per horizon were recollected. Samples were\n      processed for gamma and chemical separation of Sr-90 in IF and NIR.",
